Z||000000||Zoom88||11-26-2001||07:57 AM||||Almost have the Side scoop installation completed just need to reattach the molding.<BR>I bought the scoops from: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/parts.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/parts.html</A> <BR> I love them !! bolted right up without having to do any mods to them....great work !<BR>Anyone looking to add these you will not go wrong getting them from Fierowarehouse, price, service and response time was very good in my opinion. Now if I can just get him or the fibersmith to make me a rear deck lid scoop just for the notchback with the hump in the lid that doesn't require cutting the entire hump out (lose to much structural support in the lid, just my opinion) then I would be on cloud 9 !!!!||||reg||10
Z||000001||Sage||11-26-2001||10:06 AM||||Terry,<P>Thanks for the kind words.  Very glad you got them installed with no hitches.  We tried very hard to make them so they fit the way they should and so you don't have to spend hours getting them ready to go on.<P>Can't tell you how glad I am that your experience was good, and can't thank you enough for the positive feedback.<P> Also, can't wait to see some pics when you're all done!  <P>There are other projects in the works, but can't say what they are or when they will be available.  Will let you know what and when as time passes.<P>Thanks again, good show!<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Edited to add:<P>Thanks Kevin and Dave for your input!  Just a footnote: revin bought his "straight out of the mold" so had to do all the finishing work, including drilling all the holes, sanding and paint prep, so that's how he got them cheaper!  We have stopped offering this option, as there is just too much potential for mishap.  Not a cut to anybody, it's just that it takes some bodywork experience to properly get these things ready and finished to go on your car.<P>  If anyone is interested in them in that condition, drop me or Doug a note and we will see if we can work something out for you.<P>Kevin, got any pics of the finished product?  Oreif allready posted his, in fact, we put his car on the web page,as it is a beautiful Fiero, with or without sidescoops!  Thanks Dave.<BR>------------------<BR>Have a good one!<p>[This message has been edited by Sage (edited 11-26-2001).]||||reg||14
